Important: this is a DARK theme — `--cp-ink: var(--rp-paper)` (paper = light text on dark). `--rp-verified: #35d0ae` (bright teal), `--rp-money: #f4b740` (bright amber). Dim variants are rgba with alpha (used for borders mostly). So badge text in `--rp-verified` (#35d0ae) on dark ghost bg = high contrast ✓. Use full-strength accents for badge text.

Now — line 1760-1766 shows an existing pattern: `.something { border-color: var(--rp-verified); background: var(--rp-verified-ghost); color: var(--rp-verified); }` — likely a "verified" chip style. My chip-goal can mirror that.

